    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) leading the charge against May. **Gunnar Henderson** represents our premier play, bolstered by a 16% park adjustment and a significant platoon advantage that keeps his efficiency ceiling high. We are also leaning heavily into **Jackson Merrill** (71.96) and **Kyle Tucker** (70.26); both benefit from favorable matchups against RHP Tyler Phillips and LHP Cesar Perdomo, respectively. **Heliot Ramos** (67.58) remains a high-value start in this environment, as his performance against LHP Eduardo Rodriguez is aided by the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a meaningful boost to our pursuit of stolen bases\u2014the scarcest commodity in our pursuit of the Roto crown.\n\nStrategic adjustments for the day revolve around navigating the volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Heliot Ramos**. While **Miguel Vargas** (64.71) draws a favorable look against A. Sears due to a strong xwOBA, the toughest decision on the bench was **Josh Jung** (42.88). Despite a respectable score, he fell just short of the starting threshold due to the elite efficiency of Cease, whose sub-3.00 xERA profile suppressed the offensive potential of the entire matchup. Similarly, while we considered **Henry Bolte** (41.36) for his leadoff spot, the sheer dominance of Espino on the mound made him a liability compared to the high-floor production we expect from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.25) and **Drake Baldwin** (61.03). We will monitor the confirmed lineups closely, specifically ensuring that **Wade Meckler**\u2014currently sitting at a marginal 41.66\u2014remains protected if the L/L platoon disadvantage persists.",
